{"topic": "HTTP and HTTPS", "part": {"part": 1, "title": "HTTP request and response structure", "duration_target": 45, "script": "HTTP is a text\u2011based protocol where a client asks for a resource and a server returns it. The client sends a line with a method like GET, a path, and then header lines. The server replies with a status code, its own headers, and an optional body containing the resource. Both sides use TCP on port 80 to transport these messages.", "visual_plan": ["Show client and server boxes", "Draw request arrow with method, path, headers", "Draw response arrow with status, headers, body"], "scenes": [{"scene_id": "s1", "narration": "HTTP is a text\u2011based protocol where a client asks for a resource and a server returns it.", "clear": false, "elements": [{"id": "title", "type": "TEXT", "animation": "WRITE", "x": 50.0, "y": 8.0, "w": null, "h": null, "text": "HTTP Request/Response", "label": "", "size": "title", "color": "ink", "from_id": "", "to_id": "", "x2": null, "y2": null, "steps": [], "direction": "horizontal", "rows": [], "nodes": [], "edges": [], "target": "", "page": null, "to_x": null, "to_y": null}, {"id": "client", "type": "BOX", "animation": "DRAW", "x": 20.0, "y": 30.0, "w": 20.0, "h": 12.0, "text": "", "label": "Client", "size": "normal", "color": "blue", "from_id": "", "to_id": "", "x2": null, "y2": null, "steps": [], "direction": "horizontal", "rows": [], "nodes": [], "edges": [], "target": "", "page": null, "to_x": null, "to_y": null}, {"id": "server", "type": "BOX", "animation": "DRAW", "x": 80.0, "y": 30.0, "w": 20.0, "h": 12.0, "text": "", "label": "Server", "size": "normal", "color": "green", "from_id": "", "to_id": "", "x2": null, "y2": null, "steps": [], "direction": "horizontal", "rows": [], "nodes": [], "edges": [], "target": "", "page": null, "to_x": null, "to_y": null}]}, {"scene_id": "s2", "narration": "The client sends a line with a method like GET, a path, and then header lines.", "clear": false, "elements": [{"id":